.venv
# Every env file, not just the one named `.env`.
#
# `.env` matches that exact name and nothing else, so `.env.test` - which
# carries the test environment's database password - was committable. Found by
# running `git check-ignore` before creating it rather than after.
#
# The templates are the exception: they are the documentation of what has to be
# set, and they carry placeholders.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.test.example
**/sql/logs
**/sql/target
**/sql/dbt_packages
**/sql/.user.yml
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/logs
.nox
.tmp*
*.vscode
.idea/
.dlt/secrets.toml
*.py[cod]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info
.DS_Store
# AH member tokens written by bonuschef.utils.ah_login / AHTokenManager
ah_tokens.json
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Local Claude Code settings. Untracked and machine-specific: one of these was
# rsynced onto the deployment host, where it made `git describe` report the
# checkout dirty -- so a clean v1.3.0 deployment announced itself as "geen
# release" on account of an editor preference file.
.claude/settings.local.json
